[38.443267, "o", "---\r\n\r\n## Preflight Result: 🚫 BLOCK\r\n\r\n**Upgrade must not proceed.**\r\n\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Verdict** | `BLOCK` |\r\n| **Fingerprint** | `67c8f02774972c195947d2e4183295c9372bb96c8cbc92f042a689191d862010` |\r\n| **Tool** | helm-agent-preflight v0.1.0 (commit `91250d3`) |\r\n| **No deployment occurred** | ✅ confirmed |\r\n| **Evidence completeness** | COMPLETE |\r\n| **Rendering stable** | ✅ yes |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Diff Summary\r\n\r\n| Added | Modified | Removed |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| 0 | 1 | 0 |\r\n\r\nThe only change is to `ClusterRole/webapp-reader` — its `$.rules` were replaced entirely.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Security Findings\r\n\r\n#### [CRITICAL] RBAC-001 — `ClusterRole/webapp-reader` (new, not pre-existing)\r\n- **Path:** `$.rules[0].resources`\r\n- **Meaning:** The candidate sets `resources: [\"*\"]`, granting this ClusterRole access to **every resource type** in the cluster (Pods, Secrets, ConfigMaps, PersistentVolumes, etc.). This is a privilege escalation from the baseline, which only allowed `pods` and `services`.\r\n\r\n#### [CRITICAL] RBAC-002 — `ClusterRole/webapp-reader` (new, not pre-existing)\r\n- **Path:** `$.rules[0].verbs`\r\n- **Meaning:** The candidate sets `verbs: [\"*\"]`, granting **every operation** (get, list, watch, create, update, patch, delete, escalate, bind…). The baseline was read-only (`get`, `list`, `watch`). Combined with the wildcard resources, this effectively grants cluster-admin-equivalent permissions to anything bound to this role.\r\n\r\nBoth findings are **introduced by this upgrade** (`pre_existing: false`).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Fix: Exact Diff\r\n\r\nRevert `examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/rbac.yaml` to explicit, least-privilege rules:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n--- a/examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/rbac.yaml\r\n+++ b/examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/rbac.yaml\r\n rules:\r\n-  - apiGroups: [\"*\"]\r\n-    resources: [\"*\"]\r\n-    verbs: [\"*\"]\r\n+  - apiGroups: [\"\"]\r\n+    resources: [\"pods\", \"services\"]\r\n+    verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis restores the exact baseline posture. If the candidate genuinely needs access to additional resources or verbs, enumerate them explicitly — **never use `*`** in production RBAC rules.\r\n\r\n> ⚠️ **Do not run `helm upgrade` until a PASS verdict is obtained against the fixed chart.** Human authorization is required before modifying the candidate chart.\r\n"]
